{"name":"Hot Brown","hex":"#984218","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot brown","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An open sandwich of turkey and bacon, covered in mornay sauce and baked or broiled until the bread is crisp and the sauce begins to brown."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot Brown","blocks":[{"text":"A Hot Brown sandwich is an American hot sandwich originally created at the Brown Hotel in Louisville, Kentucky, by Fred K. Schmidt in 1926. It is a variation of traditional Welsh rarebit and was one of two signature sandwiches created by chefs at the Brown Hotel shortly after its founding in 1923. It was created to serve as an alternative to ham and egg late-night dinners."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Hot_Brown%2C_Brown_Hotel.jpg/330px-Hot_Brown%2C_Brown_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Brown","wikidata":"Q5909823"},{"title":"Hot (James Brown album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot is the 42nd studio album by American musician James Brown. The album was released in January of 1976 by Polydor Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e6/James_Brown_Hot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_(James_Brown_album)","wikidata":"Q20715588"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wi